Fluid and Electrolytes\
\uc0\u61623  Signs of Fluid Volume Deficit: Dry mucous membranes, poor skin turgor, oliguria,\
tachycardia, hypotension.\
\uc0\u61623  Hypervolemia Signs: Bounding pulse, edema, JVD, crackles in lungs.\
\uc0\u61623  Electrolyte Basics:\
o Potassium: Primarily intracellular; hyperkalemia may cause arrhythmias.\
o Magnesium: Linked to tremors, confusion if low; found in intracellular fluid.\
o Sodium/Chloride: Extracellular; check sodium for neuro changes.\
o Hypocalcemia Signs: Muscle twitching, tetany, Chvostek\'92s sign.\
\uc0\u61623  Key Terms:\
o Osmotic Pressure: Increased in hyperglycemia (DKA).\
o Oncotic Pressure: Related to fluid in the abdominal cavity (ascites).\
o Metabolic Acidosis: Potassium shifts out of cells, increasing hyperkalemia risk.\
2. Catheterization and CAUTI Prevention\
\uc0\u61623  CAUTI Prevention: Remove Foley ASAP, use aseptic technique.\
\uc0\u61623  Determining Foley Size: Measured in French.\
\uc0\u61623  Measuring Intake & Output: Essential for monitoring fluid balance.\
3. Gastrointestinal Disorders\
\uc0\u61623  GERD Management: Small frequent meals, avoid hot/spicy foods, no eating 2-3 hours\
before bed, PPIs, prokinetic agents, elevate head of bed, avoid fatty foods, caffeine,\
chocolate, alcohol.\
\uc0\u61623  Crohn\'92s Disease: Assess stool and dehydration; corticosteroids for inflammation.\
\uc0\u61623  Pancreatitis:\
o Symptoms: Severe LUQ or epigastric pain radiating to back; knee-chest position\
relieves pain.\
o Treatment: Opioids (morphine, fentanyl), anticholinergics, gastric acid reducers,\
pancreatic enzymes for chronic cases.\
\uc0\u61623  Diverticulitis: Low-residue diet, avoid seeds.\
4. Reproductive Health\
\uc0\u61623  Myasthenia Gravis: Persistent fatigue, muscle weakness affecting eyes, face,\
swallowing.\
\uc0\u61623  Prostate Gland Function: Provides nutrients to sperm.\
\uc0\u61623  BPH: Evaluate symptoms and monitor.\
5. Pregnancy and Neonatal Care\
\uc0\u61623  GTPAL: Gravida (G), Term (T), Preterm (P), Abortions (A), Living children (L).\
\uc0\u61623  Placenta Previa: Placenta close to cervix.\
\uc0\u61623  HELLP Syndrome: Thrombocytopenia, elevated liver enzymes, low platelets.\
messages.downloaded_by\
lOMoARcPSD|5060599\
\uc0\u61623  Hyperemesis Gravidarum: Severe vomiting, dehydration, electrolyte imbalance.\
\uc0\u61623  Postpartum Hemorrhage: Assess and treat using uterine massage, methylergonovine\
(Methargine).\
\uc0\u61623  Involution: Organs returning to pre-pregnancy state.\
\uc0\u61623  Effacement: Cervical thinning, measured in %.\
\uc0\u61623  Cerclage: Prevents preterm labor by supporting an incompetent cervix.\
\uc0\u61623  Hydatidiform Mole: No fetal heart activity; monitor HcG levels.\
6. Mental Health and Psych Disorders\
\uc0\u61623  Therapeutic Communication: Open-ended questions, validate feelings, ask about selfharm.\
\uc0\u61623  Depression: Screen using DSM-5; persistent sadness or low mood.\
\uc0\u61623  Suicidal Ideation: Use suicide precautions, notify HCP.\
\uc0\u61623  Generalized Anxiety Disorder: Persistent restlessness, fatigue.\
\uc0\u61623  Social Phobia: Fear of social situations, avoidance due to fear of judgment.\
\uc0\u61623  Eating Disorders:\
o Anorexia: Fear of weight gain, body dysphoria, malnutrition.\
o Bulimia: Binge-eating with compensatory behaviors (e.g., purging).\
\uc0\u61623  Psych Medications:\
o SSRI Toxicity: Never stop abruptly, monitor for suicidal thoughts, avoid St.\
John\'92s Wort.\
o Serotonin Syndrome: High fever, hyperreflexia, tachycardia.\
o MAOIs: Avoid tyramine-rich foods (aged cheese, fermented foods).\
o Lamotrigine: Treats bipolar; watch for Stevens-Johnson syndrome.\
\uc0\u61623  Schizophrenia: Hallucinations, delusions, word salad, flat affect.\
\uc0\u61623  Baker Act: Law allowing involuntary examination of individuals in mental health crises.\
7. Endocrine and Metabolic Disorders\
\uc0\u61623  Diabetes:\
o 3 P\'92s: Polyuria, polydipsia, polyphagia.\
o Type 1 Management: Lifelong insulin therapy.\
\uc0\u61623  SIADH: Treat with 3% sodium chloride for hyponatremia.\
\uc0\u61623  Hypoglycemia: Signs in infants include hypoactivity and excessive crying.\
8. Labor and Delivery\
\uc0\u61623  Stages of Labor: Monitor fetal heart rate and check for accelerations.\
\uc0\u61623  Assessing Fetal Position: Vertex indicates head-down position.\
\uc0\u61623  Intrapartum: After water breaks, check fetal heart rate to detect possible cord\
compression.\
\uc0\u61623  Postpartum:\
o Fundal Massage: For boggy uterus.\
o Fundal Height: Correlates to weeks of gestation (20 weeks at the umbilicus).\
o Lochia Stages: 6 days post-op, expect serosa discharge.\
