1. B: Breasts\
o Assess for:\
\uc0\u61607  Consistency: Soft (filling) or firm (engorgement)\
\uc0\u61607  Tenderness: Tender or nontender\
\uc0\u61607  Temperature: Warm or cool\
\uc0\u61607  Nipples: Check for cracking or breakdown\
2. U: Uterus (Fundus)\
o Immediately after delivery, the fundus should be:\
\uc0\u61607  Firm and midline\
\uc0\u61607  Measured in relation to the umbilicus (e.g., U +1, U -1)\
\uc0\u61607  6-12 hours postpartum: Fundus at the level of the umbilicus\
\uc0\u61607  Postpartum day 2: Should be U -1\
o Massage technique: Upper hand on top of fundus, lower hand supporting uterus\
above the symphysis pubis\
3. B: Bladder\
o Assess for distention:\
\uc0\u61607  Should void within 6 hours after delivery; may require straight\
catheterization if unable to void\
\uc0\u61607  If boggy and deviated, encourage bladder emptying\
4. B: Bowel\
o Bowel sounds may be hypoactive initially:\
\uc0\u61607  Expected bowel movement by day 2 or day 3\
\uc0\u61607  May need stool softeners; encourage increased fiber and fluids\
5. L: Lochia\
o Assess type and amount:\
\uc0\u61607  Type:\
\uc0\u61607  Rubra (red): 3-4 days\
\uc0\u61607  Serosa (pink): 4-10 days\
\uc0\u61607  Alba (white): 10+ days\
\uc0\u61607  Amount:\
\uc0\u61607  Scant: 1 inch stain in 1 hour\
\uc0\u61607  Light: <4 inch stain\
\uc0\u61607  Moderate: 6 inches\
\uc0\u61607  Heavy: Saturated\
o Note earthy odor; no clots should be present\
6. E: Episiotomy\
o Assess for REEDA (Redness, Edema, Ecchymosis, Drainage, Approximation):\
\uc0\u61607  Treatment: Ice for the first 24 hours, peri bottle with each void or bowel\
movement, sitz baths\
o For C-section: Assess REEDA and perform gentle fundal checks\
7. H: Hemorrhoids\
o Assess for size and swelling:\
\uc0\u61607  Treatment: Ice, Tucks, lidocaine spray\
8. E: Extremities\
o Assess for edema, pain, and pulses:\
\uc0\u61607  Palpate calves and behind the knees; check Homan\'92s sign for DVT\
