Urinary Catheterization Study Guide\
Definition:\
\uc0\u61623  A hollow tube placed through the urethra into the bladder.\
Purposes of Urinary Catheterization:\
1. Monitor strict intake and output (I&O).\
2. Relieve urinary obstruction.\
3. Provide pre-operative and post-operative care.\
4. Aid patients with neurological conditions preventing complete bladder emptying.\
5. Assess post-void residual when a bladder scanner is unavailable.\
Types of Catheters:\
1. Straight Catheter: Single lumen for short-term use.\
2. Double Lumen Catheter: Indwelling retention catheter for long-term use.\
3. Triple Lumen Catheter: For continuous closed irrigation.\
French Measurement:\
\uc0\u61623  Foley catheters are measured in French units (1 French = 0.33 mm).\
o An 18 French catheter is approximately 6 mm in diameter.\
