\uc0\u61623  Size Guidelines:\
1. Children: 8-10 FR.\
2. Females and Males: 14-16 FR.\
3. Males with Enlarged Prostate: May need a smaller size or a coude catheter\
(slightly bent tip) to bypass obstructions.\
4. Post-Urological Surgery: Larger sizes may be used to facilitate hematuria and\
clot passage.\
Suprapubic Catheters:\
\uc0\u61623  Indicated for patients with:\
o Enlarged prostates.\
o Urethral strictures.\
o Post-urologic surgery.\
\uc0\u61623  Care: Clean around the catheter with aseptic technique in a circular motion (cleanest to\
dirtiest).\
Pericare Importance:\
\uc0\u61623  Essential to prevent urinary tract infections (UTIs).\
\uc0\u61623  Mandatory prior to catheter insertion.\
CAUTI (Catheter-Associated Urinary Tract Infection)\
Prevention Strategies:\
1. Use catheters only when absolutely necessary.\
2. Insert catheters using sterile technique.\
3. Maintain urinary catheters:\
o Perform perineal care regularly.\
o Ensure no kinks in the tubing.\
o Keep the drainage bag below the bladder.\
o Monitor for signs and symptoms of UTI.\
4. Remove catheters as soon as possible.\
