What is RhoGam?\
\uc0\u61623  Definition: RhoGam is an immune globulin injection used to prevent Rh incompatibility\
between an Rh-negative mother and an Rh-positive baby.\
\uc0\u61623  Source: Made from human blood.\
\uc0\u61623  Importance:\
o Most people are Rh-negative.\
o If both parents are Rh-negative, the baby will be Rh-negative.\
o If both parents are Rh-positive, the baby will be Rh-positive.\
o If the mother is Rh-negative, the baby could be either Rh-positive or Rh-negative.\
Mechanism of Action\
\uc0\u61623  Rh Incompatibility: If an Rh-negative mother has an Rh-positive baby, her body may\
recognize the Rh-positive cells as foreign and produce antibodies against them.\
\uc0\u61623  Consequences:\
o Can lead to anemia, kidney failure, and shock in the fetus.\
o Antibody levels can be monitored; higher levels indicate increased risk of\
complications.\
Administration Guidelines\
\uc0\u61623  Dosage: Typically 300 mcg (may vary based on blood transfer).\
\uc0\u61623  Timing:\
o Given at 28 weeks gestation if the mother is Rh-negative.\
o Administered within 72 hours after delivery of an Rh-positive baby.\
o Administered in cases of potential blood mixing (e.g., trauma, ectopic pregnancy).\
Contraindications\
